WHY THIS FILE IS IN THIS REPO
DX-life sets --font-family-cyrillic to 'Oswald' and base/_globals.scss:35-44 switches every
h1/h2/h3 to it under [lang="ru-RU"], with letter-spacing -0.02em. That switch exists because
BEBAS NEUE HAS NO CYRILLIC GLYPHS AT ALL — their heading face simply cannot render Russian, so
without the switch a Russian heading falls out of the family entirely. Ours did exactly that:
we ship a `ru` locale, we had neither the rule nor the font, so every Russian heading rendered
in whatever condensed system face the browser chose.

WHICH SUBSETS, AND WHY FOUR
cyrillic and cyrillic-ext are the point. latin and latin-ext are carried too because a Russian
heading routinely contains Latin characters — a country name, a figure, an ampersand — and a
face that covers only Cyrillic drops those glyphs back to the fallback MID-WORD, which looks
worse than not switching at all. Google's own unicode-range values are carried verbatim
(css2 v57), so the browser fetches only the subset a given heading needs.

    oswald-400-cyrillic.woff2      6700 B
    oswald-400-cyrillic-ext.woff2  7688 B
    oswald-400-latin.woff2        12248 B
    oswald-400-latin-ext.woff2    11624 B

Each verified to begin with the wOF2 magic (774f4632) after download, because a fetch that
silently returns an HTML error page also "succeeds" and a font that is really a 404 page fails
at render time with no network error to find later.

Weight 400 only: their --font-weight-regular is what h1/h2/h3 use, and nothing on the regions
surfaces asks Oswald for another weight.

